  "body": "#1098 (#1091, the stock-top re-reading of vertical dives) has merged (0fc30b65); this branch has merged it from main, so the diff is this PR's own change only.\r\n\r\n#1095: the rapid-in-stock law caps every column at the stock's highest point. #1098 re-reads a convicted vertical dive against the stock and part solids under the tool stack; lateral rapids kept the flat cap. A drill's link from hole to hole at its retract plane (Z 22), across the low part (Z 20) of a stepped from-model casting with a boss to Z 30 elsewhere, was convicted as if the boss stood under it, and the post was blocked.\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.18.0, PROCESS_VERSION 26; merged with upstream main at 62a2c93a (head ca791ed2).\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **`sim::verify::stock_top::acquit_by_stock_top`** now also re-reads an upright LATERAL rapid:\r\n  - Each band of the stack (flute, shank, holder) is read over the capsule it sweeps along the move, against the highest vertex of any stock or part facet whose plan comes within its radius. This is the same upper bound as the dive's disc: for a closed shell, the topmost surface over a point is on a facet covering it.\r\n  - The tip is taken at the rapid's lowest end for the whole move. A climbing or falling traverse is judged as if it ran level at its low end, which can only over-report.\r\n  - Like the dive, it only removes convictions. It keeps the conviction for an open or non-manifold shell, a non-finite end, a posed rapid, a column-free mode (radial, revolve, rotary), or a flute capsule that meets no facet.\r\n- New `dist2_seg_tri`: the plan distance from a segment to a triangle. A dive is the zero-length capsule. `dist2_seg_tri` of a point returns `dist2_tri` of it, float for float, so every dive verdict is unchanged.\r\n- **Changed pin (#1098's):** `only_upright_column_dives_are_re_read` asserted that \"a lateral rapid is never re-read\", which is this issue's gap. Its diagonal dive to Z 22 over the low step, with the boss 7 mm past its end, is now acquitted. The same move posed stays convicted.\r\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1095-lateral-rapid-stock-top.md`.\r\n\r\n## How it was tested\r\n\r\nNew pinning tests:\r\n- `crates/app/tests/stepped_stock_link.rs`: a part-sourced Drill of two holes in the part's open cavity, under a from-model casting stock, linking at the Z 22 retract plane.\r\n  - `a_link_over_the_low_part_of_a_stepped_stock_passes_and_posts`: on the old law this fails (the link is `RapidInStock` and the post is blocked); now it passes and posts.\r\n  - `the_same_link_across_the_boss_is_convicted`: convicted and post blocked.\r\n  - `a_boss_under_the_tool_rim_along_the_link_is_convicted`: the boss 1 mm beside the centre line, under the 2 mm rim between the holes.\r\n- `sim::verify::stock_top::tests` (5 new):\r\n  - `a_traverse_over_the_low_step_is_acquitted`: along X, toward the boss along Y, and a falling traverse.\r\n  - `a_traverse_crossing_the_boss_stands`: including one climbing over it.\r\n  - `a_boss_under_the_rim_along_the_way_stands`.\r\n  - `a_holder_band_over_the_boss_along_the_way_stands`.\r\n  - `a_traverse_reads_the_part_and_fails_closed_like_a_dive`.\r\n- #1098's own suites are unchanged and green: `stepped_stock_rapid`, `ladder_entry_height`, and the existing `stock_top` unit tests.\r\n\r\nGates:\r\n- `cargo xtask gate batch` on 7e8d92cf (18.3 min): all green. That is geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion (slow suites included), app (`center_cut_multiaxis` included), ui and clippy `-D warnings`.\r\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\r\n\r\n## Review round (7e8d92cf)\r\n\r\n- Merged main, which carries #1098's final rules. The conflicting line, the dive's `clear_of` call, keeps both sides: the `(c, c)` point trace and main's `m.to.z - e`.\r\n- The lateral branch takes the same rules: the tip at `low - e`. `bands(tool, e)` (radii grown by `e`, the wider of holder and shank above the shank) and the non-finite-excess refusal came in with the merge and apply to both paths.\r\n- New pin: `stock_top::tests::a_traverse_takes_the_coarse_models_excess_like_a_dive`. A link 0.3 mm over the meshed low step, and a link with its rim 0.3 mm short of the boss, are clear at excess 0 and convicted at 0.5. A NaN excess keeps the conviction. It fails with the lateral tip left at `low`, which was checked.\r\n- `stepped_stock_link.rs` now keeps the casting in the tree as raw stock only (`SetStockSourceOnly`, #1094), as `stepped_stock_rapid.rs` does. Since #1056, a from-model stock whose deleted source leaves an unknown chord is never re-read, so the old deleted-casting fixture no longer reached the law.\r\n- Tests on ca791ed2: `cargo test -p camcraft-sim`, all green (19 `stock_top` tests). App `stepped_stock_link` 3, `stepped_stock_rapid` 8, `ladder_entry_height` 4: all pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets` and `-p camcraft-app --test stepped_stock_link`, `-D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- A stock-sourced op with no judged stock solid (Drill, Face or the Pocket family from `SrcRef::Stock`) is not re-read. Its column law reads the op's region in the stock's place, and #1098's wiring (`stock_top_law::acquit`) returns before any re-reading. That is #1098's design. This PR keeps it and pins the issue's own case, a model-sourced op over a from-model stock.\r\n- Tilted-frame (indexed) setups: the lateral re-reading is upright-only by construction. A posed rapid keeps its conviction (pinned in `a_traverse_reads_the_part_and_fails_closed_like_a_dive`); no test pins an upright rapid in a tilted plane's local frame.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Rapid check: a rapid moving sideways under the clearance plane over a stepped stock is judged against the stock really under it, not the stock's highest point (#1095)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (the issue's label). Not escalated.\r\n\r\nFixes #1095\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
